    "adaptation": "Demon Beast 1 is a reviewed visual adaptation for the bounded canonical Dretch, not a vendor identification. Historical Attack1/2/5/6 aliases remain available; current rig-scoped Bite and Claws profiles select Attack 2 and Attack 3 respectively with their reviewed frame-6 contacts; there is no ranged mapping. Fifteen meaningful 128 px columns, eight visually reviewed E, SE, S, SW, W, NW, N, NE rows. The PNG-only package declares no FPS/pivot. 12 fps and support pixel (64,83), origin_y_from_ground 45, are execution adaptations informed by the separate idle shadow centroid (~63.5,82.6). Separate shadow alpha 0.5 reuses the fixed-rig appearance policy. No effects, block variants or full package imported.",
    "summoning_body_review": {
      "date": "2026-10-03",
      "source_variant": "Demon Beast 1",
      "direction_evidence": "Same eight-row convention as installed Demon Beast 1/2/3; reviewed Idle/body silhouettes.",
      "timing": "15 original samples at authored 12 FPS. The PNG packs provide no FPS, pivot or event markers. Contact/recovery frames below are reviewed execution choices.",
      "ground_pivot": {
        "x": 64.0,
        "y": 83,
        "evidence": "Retained existing rig pivot."
      },
      "shadow_policy": "Original separate shadow sheets at existing fixed-rig alpha 0.5.",
      "attacks": {
        "dretch_bite": {
          "source_clip": "Attack 2",
          "contact_frame": 6,
          "recover_frame": 11,
          "motion": "Existing generic body/head lunge adapted to Bite; no literal vendor Bite strip exists."
        },
        "dretch_claws": {
          "source_clip": "Attack 3",
          "contact_frame": 6,
          "recover_frame": 11,
          "motion": "Cross-body claw extension at 6."
        }
      },
      "outcomes": "Hit, miss, critical, opportunity and native Multiattack children select the same explicit anatomical row. One emitted attack fact owns one contact; art turns and repeated swipes create no extra native hits. Separate AttackVfx tracks are explicitly empty.",
      "movement": "Run owns the gait only. Native recorded path/height owns displacement. Jump uses Rolling as an explicitly normalized pack jump/roll adaptation. Window uses CrouchWalk with its own frame keys and existing connector passage scale.",
      "flight": "No flying native capability is granted by this binding.",
      "prone": "Intact non-exploding fall, explicit frame-14 living rest pose, reverse stand-up. Death continues to use the compatible shared death owner; summoned departure is separate.",
      "ordinary_actions": "Body action, recovery, equipment, healing and optional save-avoidance gestures explicitly disabled with neutral Idle. Existing native effects, feedback and child joins remain authoritative. Shove uses the primary physical strike; forced movement uses TakeDamage brace 5.",
      "unarmed": "Rig-scoped unarmed physical-strike adaptation uses the inspected primary motion; this grants no native action.",
      "validation_scope": "Original strip/direction/support inspection and typed binding checks; full live native fight, historical replay, height/occlusion and Fey material acceptance are separate packet-5 integration checks."
    },
